    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But what about the arguments from economists who say this is basically impossible to manage? They point to France's ISF tax as a failure, where it led to massive wealth outflows and people just moving their money abroad. Isn't it a bit of a stretch to say it's a \"proven\" way to boost productivity when so many experts argue it just drains the economy of the very investment it needs?",
